---
title: "attendance_recording (kintai-v3: Initial Schema)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_auth: user authenticates via Supabase Auth
    q_auth --> q_rls_check: INSERT into attendances
    q_rls_check --> q_check_owner: evaluate RLS insert policy
    q_check_owner --> q_validate_type: auth.uid() = user_id
    q_check_owner --> q_check_admin: auth.uid() != user_id
    q_check_admin --> q_validate_type: is_admin() = true
    q_check_admin --> q_deny: is_admin() = false
    q_validate_type --> q_check_constraint: CHECK type in ('in', 'out')
    q_check_constraint --> q_set_defaults: type is valid
    q_check_constraint --> q_deny: type is invalid
    q_set_defaults --> q_insert: id = gen_random_uuid(), timestamp = now(), date = (now() at time zone 'utc')::date
    q_insert --> [*]: row inserted successfully
    q_deny --> [*]: RLS or constraint violation, operation denied

    note right of q_rls_check
        INV-001: Users can only insert attendance records for themselves (auth.uid() = user_id)
        INV-002: Admins can insert attendance records for any user via is_admin() policy
        INV-003: type must be exactly 'in' or 'out' (CHECK constraint)
    end note

    note right of q_set_defaults
        INV-004: date is derived from now() at UTC timezone, ensuring consistent date grouping
        INV-005: timestamp defaults to now() with time zone for precise event recording
    end note
